file:           wezterm.terminfo (only; wezterm.lua beside it is first-party)
upstream:       https://github.com/wezterm/wezterm
path:           termwiz/data/wezterm.terminfo
commit:         e2a98e1b8af156988ad0ac778658ac27b60a55fb
license:        MIT
vendored:       2026-10-12
deployed as:    nothing; tasks/wezterm-terminfo (the Linux final hook) compiles it with
                `tic -x` into ~/.terminfo, re-running when this file's SHA256 changes.
note:           wezterm.lua sets TERM=wezterm. -x keeps the extended capabilities (Tc,
                Smulx, Setulc, Ms) that make it worth more than xterm-256color.
                Tracks upstream main, which every nightly builds from (commit is main's
                when vendored): scripts/bump-versions.sh re-vendors it when main's copy
                changes, after a tic -x check, and updates commit and vendored here.
                Never hand-edit.
